# Generator output. Checkpoints keep only what a person writes or is handed;
# running IPCraft's Generate in a checkpoint recreates these files, and they are
# not committed because they drift from the generator over time. The board
# files are not listed. The user-owned core (rtl/led_controller_avmm_core.vhd)
# is committed from 06 on; in 04 and 05 it is still the generated skeleton.
/04-*/rtl/led_controller_avmm_core.vhd
/05-*/rtl/led_controller_avmm_core.vhd
/*/.vscode/settings.json
/*/.ipcraft/baseline/
/*/altera/led_controller_avmm.sdc
/*/altera/led_controller_avmm_hw.tcl
/*/altera/led_controller_avmm_project.tcl
/*/altera/test.qsys
/*/docs/led_controller_avmm_registers.md
/*/docs/*_datasheet.md
/*/rtl/led_controller_avmm.vhd
/*/rtl/led_controller_avmm_avmm.vhd
/*/rtl/led_controller_avmm_pkg.vhd
/*/rtl/led_controller_avmm_regs.vhd
/*/tb/conftest.py
/*/tb/led_controller_avmm_test.py
/*/tb/Makefile
/*/tb/register_model.py
/*/tb/test_led_controller_avmm_sim.py
/*/tb/verification_manifest.json
